WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.350
Everybody's favorite friendly neighborhood
Spider-Man is set to swing back into theaters

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.300
come July 2019.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.660
And while audiences everywhere are all set
for another Spidey-fest, Marvel Studios sure

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.400
is taking its time doling out the details.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:19.160
For now, we'll have to settle for these previously
leaked tidbits and the ever reliable rumor

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:19.660
mill.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.380
Here's what we know, or think we know, so
far.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.580
In January 2019, we learned that Nick Fury
won't be the only S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.920
veteran returning to the MCU in Spider-Man:
Far from Home.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.840
"So nice to finally meet you, Spider-Man."

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.960
"You're Nick Fury."

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.640
The first Far from Home teaser trailer contained
a brief shot that showed a pair of characters

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.070
who seemed to be former S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:52.330
Agent Maria Hill and Nick Fury being attacked
by an Elemental, but fans were not entirely

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.820
sure... until actress Cobie Smulders set the
record straight.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:01.180
She posted a screenshot of herself and Samuel
L. Jackson on Instagram, writing in the photo's

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:01.700
caption:

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:02.560
"It's me!

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.140
It's me!

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:03.940
I swear...

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.260
[The] one on the left… no not the monster…
the one with the ponytail."

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:12.280
Obviously, Smulders was joking about anyone
confusing her with what appears to be a massive

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:17.860
sand creature, though ironically the last
time we saw Smulders as Maria Hill was in

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:22.420
Avengers: Infinity War's post-credits scene
when Hill and her old boss Fury were both

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.360
"dusted" by Thanos' decimation.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.780
So… maybe she wasn't joking.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.840
Throughout 2017's Spider-Man: Homecoming,
every attempt by Peter Parker to contact Tony

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:38.140
Stark or the Avengers was filtered through
Stark's pal Happy Hogan, portrayed by MCU

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.480
veteran Jon Favreau.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:44.460
We missed out on seeing Happy in Avengers:
Infinity War, so there was some question as

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:49.300
to whether or not the guy whose favorite pastime
was ignoring Peter Parker would be around

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.300
for Far from Home.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.180
"This is you."

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.300
"Oh, we're neighbors?"

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.300
"We're not roommates.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:54.620
Suit up."

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.360
"Okay, Peter, you got this, you got this."

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:57.420
"What the hell are you wearing?"

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:04.010
We got our first inkling that Happy was returning
in September 2018, when a Reddit user posted

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:07.420
a video that appeared to show Favreau on the
set of Far from Home.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:13.689
The return of Happy was finally confirmed
in January 2019 with the release of the first

00:02:13.689 --> 00:02:17.970
Spider-Man: Far from Home teaser trailer,
which featured, among other things, Happy

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.500
getting flirty with Aunt May.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.260
"You look nice."

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:20.780
"Thank you!

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:21.420
You too."

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:21.920
"Thank you.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:22.860
New dress?"

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:23.500
"Yes, it is.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.340
How'd you know?"

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.380
"What just happened?"

00:02:28.389 --> 00:02:32.840
It will be interesting to see how, if at all,
Happy's new interest in Parker's aunt will

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.020
affect the way he treats the young hero.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.180
We doubt it.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:42.659
September 2018 was a big month for rumors
and spoilers for Spider-Man: Far from Home,

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.500
but not all of them were accurate.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.760
Along with the set video that leaked Jon Favreau,
it was the month SuperBroMovies reported that

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.300
Gwyneth Paltrow would appear in Far from Home
as Pepper Potts.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:58.980
While Robert Downey Jr. and Jon Favreau had
larger roles in Spider-Man: Homecoming, Paltrow

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.620
appeared briefly in the film's final moments
for the Spider-Man press conference that never

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.120
happened.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.880
"Did you guys screw this up?"

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.150
"He told the kid to go wait in the car."

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:08.200
"Are you kidding me?

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.390
I have a room full of people in there waiting
for some big announcement.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.440
What am I gonna tell them?"

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.820
We've since heard that the rumor of Pepper's
return in July's Far From Home was a false

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:17.320
one.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:23.480
In February 2019, Paltrow told Variety that
April's Avengers: Endgame will be her last

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.000
film as part of the MCU, at least for the
near future.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.520
Paltrow told Variety:

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.340
"I mean, I'm a bit old to be in a suit and
all that at this point."

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.800
But she didn't discount a brief return in
the future.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.360
Paltrow went on to say, quote, "Of course,
if they said, 'Can you come back for a day?,'

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.220
I will always be there if they need me."

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:48.180
The tragic Gwen Stacy, the girl Peter Parker
loved but couldn't save, was played by Bryce

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.020
Dallas Howard in 2007's Spider-Man 3.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:55.660
Next, Emma Stone took the role for the two
Andrew Garfield Spidey films.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.580
With everything already going on in Spider-Man:
Far from Home, it doesn't necessarily seem

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:03.020
like the ideal fit for her introduction.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:09.980
But ideal fit or not, in December 2017 a number
of supposed audition tapes surfaced with different

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:14.900
actresses claiming to be vying for the part
of Gwen Stacy in the next Spider-Man movie.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:20.060
Iris Haller, whose only credited work is for
a German soap opera, is one of the apparent

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:20.840
hopefuls.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:25.860
Another auditioning actress introduces herself
only as "Luna" and speaks with what appears

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.880
to be a thick French accent.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:32.640
Since the tapes were leaked, there's been
no word on Gwen Stacy appearing in Far from

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:33.140
Home.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:37.780
Maybe the recordings were intentional red
herrings, maybe they were fakes, but time

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:38.780
will tell for sure.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:44.860
Early in November 2018, Marvel launched a
clock counting down the 240 days until the

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.620
July 2019 release of Spider-Man: Far from
Home.

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:54.440
That specific number has some fans claiming
that Miles Morales, the version of Spider-Man

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:59.440
featured in 2018's Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse,
could be appearing in Far from Home.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:00.800
"C'mon dude, let's go.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:03.520
Miles!"

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.340
Why is the number 240 significant, you ask?

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:13.780
It just so happens that acclaimed writer and
Miles Morales creator Brian Michael Bendis

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:19.480
ended his tenure with Marvel's Spider-Man
with issue #240 in May 2018.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.979
That's all it took to get fans speculating
whether there was a connection between the

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:24.700
two numbers.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:28.640
That's not much of a confirmation that Morales
will be in Far from Home.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:31.180
It could just be a coincidence, after all.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:36.060
On the other hand, considering the undeniable
success of Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.970
as well as the fact that a deleted Spider-Man:
Homecoming scene mentioned a character Miles

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:41.460
by name…

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:42.960
"Yeah, sorry, Miles.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:43.480
I'm...

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.520
I'm not gonna make it.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:45.860
Yeah, I'm just stuck."

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:51.880
… the notion of Morales appearing alongside
Tom Holland's Peter Parker may be less a question

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:53.960
of if than a question of when.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:00.960
In August 2018, The Wrap reported that Crazy
Rich Asians actor Remy Hii had been cast in

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.900
Spider-Man: Far from Home… as, well, someone.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.920
Nobody seems to be entirely sure who yet.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:11.960
Just about every noteworthy Spider-Man bad
guy has been rumored to be appearing in Spider-Man:

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.840
Far from Home at one point or another.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:18.800
So, with the exception of Vulture or Mysterio,
Hii could be portraying just about any of

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:19.300
them.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.740
On the other hand; the Australian actor's
Chinese ancestry, the martial arts training

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:28.830
he received for his role in Netflix's Marco
Polo, Far from Home's international scope,

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:34.699
and reports of Marvel developing a film for
Shang-Chi have all fed speculation that Spider-Man:

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:38.480
Far from Home could see Remy Hii bringing
that character to the MCU.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:44.550
On the other, more plausible hand, Shang-Chi
probably isn't included in Sony's Marvel character

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:50.220
deal, so Marvel Studios might not debut an
upcoming franchise character in a Sony co-production.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:55.970
But maybe Hii could be playing Martin Li,
also known as the popular Spider-Man villain

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:56.660
Mister Negative.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:01.360
While Far From Home already seems stuffed
with villains, this film could be setting

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:06.050
up the Martin Li character, who's a family
friend to Peter and May, so he can go dark

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:06.860
in a future movie.

